{
    "background_story": "Apollo was a brilliant mathematician and logician who spent his entire career studying the works of Kurt G\u00f6del. Fascinated by G\u00f6del's incompleteness theorems, Apollo dedicated himself to understanding the implications of these groundbreaking ideas. He spent years pouring over G\u00f6del's papers, seeking to build upon his predecessor's work. Apollo's own research led to a series of innovative breakthroughs, earning him international recognition and accolades. His magnum opus, 'Beyond G\u00f6del's Limits,' explored the boundaries of mathematical certainty and challenged conventional wisdom. Apollo's work not only advanced the field of mathematics but also inspired a new generation of thinkers to grapple with the fundamental nature of truth and knowledge.",
